# deml — Cursor rules (design system)

You are working in the DEML control-plane repo. Visual design is owned by **deml-ui**.

## LOCKED STYLE — MANDATORY EVERYWHERE

**new-from-the-start (warm ash)** is the **only** allowed visual style for all DEML
product UI. **Any deviation is forbidden.** Do not invent parallel palettes, fonts,
chart contracts, or app-local design-system chrome. Expand only inside deml-ui.

## Design system (required)

- **SoT:** published npm package `deml-ui` (`^1.1.0`+); expand visuals only in the deml-ui repo.
- **Look:** **new-from-the-start (warm ash)** — mandatory; expand from that system only.
- **Palette:** dark ground `#35312D` / surface `#1C1916` / cream modules `#F3F0EA`; light ground `#D4CEC5`; primary `#2F5F8F`; accents `#3F6B54` / `#9E3D47`; muted `#C6C0B7` / `#4A453F`.
- **Type:** **Geist only** (display, marks, intro, body). No Syne / Fraunces / Inter product stacks.
- **Layout:** 8px grid, dual `data-theme`, equal `--tile-gap`, fluid dash-rows `minmax(--tile-row-unit, auto)`, solid opaque navbar, no page overflow.
- **Charts:** fixed `--chart-aspect: 2.4`, equal `--chart-inset`, width-driven height; never squash, stretch, or theme-invert series.
- **Docs:** `THEME.md` (locked contract), `docs/DEML_UI.md`, `AGENTS.md` (deml-ui Uniformity Law).
- **Storybook:** https://ui.deml.app

## Do

- Compose product pages with `app-banner`, `app-page-section`, `app-section-header`, `app-tile-board`, `app-dashboard-grid`, `app-card-grid`, `app-stat-card`, `app-chart-card`, `app-area-chart`, `app-bar-chart`, `app-site-footer`, `app-navbar`, `app-theme-toggle`.
- Keep Angular wrappers under `src/app/components` with `ViewEncapsulation.None` and **no** component CSS for design-system chrome.
- Use deml-ui CSS variables (`--color-*`, `--space-*`, `--tile-*`, `--chart-*`, `--navbar-*`).
- Preserve chart aspect (`--chart-aspect`); never squash or stretch plots.
- Prefer WCAG 2.0 AA: focus-visible, contrast, hit targets, reduced motion.

## Do not (forbidden)

- Deviate from NFTS warm ash for experiments, “atelier,” cold seven-color locks, or hybrids.
- Use or restore **Viking-UI** (`packages/viking-ui`, `@dataengineeringformachinelearning/viking-ui`, `viking-*`, `--viking-*`).
- Replace warm ash with void-black / electric `#2176ff` or a parallel frankenstein palette.
- Add Material, Bootstrap, Tailwind utility styling, or a parallel local design system.
- Hand-edit `backend/static/deml-ui.css` — sync from deml-ui via `scripts/sync_deml_ui_static.sh`.
- Put product UI back under `frontend/` (that folder is a Vercel rootDirectory shim only).
- Fix layout squash with fixed-only `grid-auto-rows` — keep `minmax(..., auto)`.
- Use see-through / frosted navbar shells over content.

## When changing visuals

1. Edit deml-ui `components/` + `styles/tokens.css` / `styles/base.css` (warm ash NFTS).
2. `npm run build` in deml-ui (dist is consumed by github installs).
3. Bump deml’s `deml-ui` dependency / lockfile.
4. Sync Django static if templates need the new CSS.
5. Run `npm run check:nfts` — must pass. CI and pre-commit enforce the same gate.

## Automated enforcement (no escape hatches)

`scripts/check_nfts_style.mjs` (`npm run check:nfts`) **fails** on:
- `styleUrl` / `styleUrls` / component `styles` under `src/app`
- Any `.css` under `src/app` or non-comment rules in `src/styles.css`
- Hardcoded hex in product TS/HTML/CSS (theme bootstrap allowlist only: NFTS palette in `src/index.html` + `ThemeService`)
- `viking-*` / `--viking-*` / Viking packages
- Missing `deml-ui/dist/styles/deml-ui.css` in `angular.json`
- `backend/static/deml-ui.css` out of sync with the installed package
- Syne / Fraunces / Google Fonts CDN in product sources
- Material / Bootstrap / Tailwind / Viking styling dependencies

Reject any PR or commit that bypasses this gate.
